 * kitgrid sits between Tailwind's base and utilities, so preflight never strips component
 * styles and your utility classes always win. The kg-* theme (bg-kg-surface, shadow-kg-sheet,
 * text-kg-ink, ...) becomes available to your own markup.
 *
 * Your Tailwind also scans kitgrid itself, so every class a component uses is generated in your
 * utilities layer with its state variants in the right order. Otherwise a plain utility you
 * also use (text-kg-fg-muted) would outrank the component's state rule (data-[state=active]:…).
 */
@layer theme, base, kg, components, utilities;

@import "./styles.css";
@import "./theme.css";

@source "./";

